{
  "slug": "docs-context",
  "name": "Docs Context",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "docs-context is the \"Super Base Context\" for Agent Coding: a structured replacement for single-file CLAUDE.md that separates project knowledge into five purpose-specific docs (architecture, modules, coding, tech-stack, decisions), loads only what the current task needs, and keeps those docs in sync with the code as a net-delta-triggered Write mode.\n\nRead mode fires before any non-trivial write/modify/refactor/design/plan task, grounding the agent in architectural constraints and conventions. Write mode fires once at the end of a task when landed changes (code, config, SQL, build scripts) differ from the doc state — no firing on read-only work, in-progress edits, or try-and-undo.\n\nWorks across Claude Code, Codex CLI, Cursor, OpenCode, Antigravity, Trae, Qoder via the standard SKILL.md format.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **2 skills**, `docs-context` (Super Base Context — project doc loader & synchronizer), `houtu-dependencies` (houtu-dependencies enterprise-grade Spring Cloud microservice foundational framework complete usage guide).\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install docs-context@claude-community` from `lujiafa/houtu-project-skills`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "antigravity",
    "codex"
  ],
  "pluginType": "wrapper",
  "wrapper": "skill",
